{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on E1 question `644ec40f`: confirmed, with one duty.\n\n1. A capability that receives a view is not refused for that reason.\n2. The shipped reads stay supported: item, page, record, records,\n   record count, scope and intent.\n3. A reached call of a port whose answer needs entry data or\n   bookkeeping data that the hypothetical view does not hold answers\n   `unavailable`, and it lacks `entry`. That covers `all()`,\n   `holders()`, `pendingRequests()`, `lookup()` and the metadata\n   fields of that kind.\n4. A port answers from the recorded view where that answer is whole.\n   `all().items` can show the same item view under the row protection.\n5. E1 projects no further port data. It adds no symbolic request, no\n   symbolic account and no second evaluator.\n6. With no hook, the runtime path and the 4,029 recorded answers stay\n   unchanged.\n\nThe duty: the implementation note lists each act of Grow, Lending and\nCounter that reaches item 3. I expect none. If one does, stop and send\nits name before the gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}